course: dictionary
lesson: 15814
title: Uncomfortably
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uncomfortably is an adverb. Adverbs tell you how something is done. It comes from comfortable, and the un- at the front means not, so uncomfortably means "not in a comfortable way".
explain: It can mean three things. It can mean your body does not feel good: «He sat uncomfortably on the hard bench.» It can mean you feel embarrassed or worried: «She laughed uncomfortably when everyone looked at her.» It can also mean too much, in a way that worries you: «The room was uncomfortably hot.»
explain: To find the meaning, read the clues around the word. Hard bench tells you about the body. Everyone looked at her tells you about feelings. Hot tells you about too much. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Uncomfortably is an adverb, and it often comes after a verb like sat, laughed or felt.
fact: «Uncomfortably» can mean that your body does not feel comfortable.
fact: «Uncomfortably» can mean that you feel embarrassed or worried.
fact: «Uncomfortably» can mean too much, as in «uncomfortably hot».
fact: Uncomfortably hot weather can be dangerous, so drink water and find some shade.
exercise: «He sat uncomfortably on the hard bench for an hour.» What does uncomfortably mean here? | Very quickly | Loudly and proudly | *In a way where his body did not feel comfortable | In a happy, relaxed way
exercise: «She laughed uncomfortably when the teacher read her name out.» What does uncomfortably suggest? | She was happy to be the loudest in class | She was very pleased and proud | *She felt embarrassed or worried | She was fast asleep
exercise: «The classroom was uncomfortably hot, so we opened the windows.» What does uncomfortably mean here? | Very quiet and calm | *Too hot, so it was a problem | Bright and cheerful | Cold and wet
test: «Mia's new shoes pinched, so she walked uncomfortably all day.» What does uncomfortably mean? | Loudly | *In a way that hurt her feet and did not feel comfortable | Without any shoes at all | Quickly and happily
test: «Tom answered the question uncomfortably, looking at the floor and going red.» What does uncomfortably suggest? | Angry with the floor | Bored and sleepy | Proud and confident | *Embarrassed and worried
exam: «The sofa was so lumpy that Grandma sat uncomfortably, shifting every minute.» Which meaning fits best? | *Her body did not feel comfortable | She felt very rich | She had far too much sleep | She was laughing at a joke
